<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kamachat Aslamie</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">17th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as King of Middag</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kamachat Aslamie was the paramount chief of the Middag chiefdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a>'s west-central plains, known from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> records as the King of Middag. He presided over a confederation of some fifteen to twenty-seven villages of the Papora, Babuza and related peoples, which kept its independence from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> longer than most of the island.</p></div>
